{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505184751,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODcxODExMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328718110"},"message":"thanks for the report... never had \"pleasure\" yet to work with AFP.\nThe main culprit, `fatal: This operation must be run in a work tree`, means that git-annex detected underlying file system as being \"crippled\" (most of the time just that it does not support symlinks) and switched mode of operation to [\"direct mode\"](https://git-annex.branchable.com/direct_mode/).  Unfortunately full support of such mode of operation is 'tricky' to say the least and we are not fully yet compatible with it.  We are expecting to support fully soon [\"v6 mode\"](https://git-annex.branchable.com/tips/unlocked_files/) of git-annex operation .  But that one we also do not fully support yet :-/  but YMMV and other @datalad/developers could chime in with more specific information","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505229403,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODg4NDk3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328884972"},"message":"Thanks for your response! I am able to create symlinks on the server (at least as far as I can tell, there are no immediately noticeable errors), so is it possible that something else is going on?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505230958,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODg5MzQ4Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328893487"},"message":"Quick update on that: when I create a directory and run `git init` and then `git annex init`, I receive the following messages:\n\n```\ninit  \n  Detected a filesystem without fifo support.\n\n  Disabling ssh connection caching.\n\n  Detected a crippled filesystem.\n\n  Disabling core.symlinks.\n\n  Enabling direct mode.\nok\n(recording state in git...)\n```\n\nBut, like I said, I can create symlinks myself without an issue.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505232078,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODg5OTUxNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328899516"},"message":"\u003e I am able to create symlinks on the server\nwhat about on the client, where you mount from the server? (I thought that it is there were datalad fails for you, not on the server)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505232998,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODkwNDE0Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328904143"},"message":"Sorry, my knowledge of the terminology isn't great. When I mount the server on my laptop and navigate to it on the terminal, I'm able to create symlinks without any problems but (from the same terminal session, same location), `git annex init` prints the above messages.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505233231,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODkwNTI1NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328905255"},"message":"Just to clarify what is happening on which machine: The output of `git annex init` you posted above, was received while creating a repository on the server, right @billbrod ?\n\nIf so, then we probably can't do much about it until support for annex V6 repositories (or direct mode) gets better (working on it). While you might be able to create symlinks (or at least something similar), git-annex apparently can't. That's something we cannot fix, since we build on top of it.\n\nDepending on the functionality of datalad you actually need