(from HasCallStack):\n  error, called at ./Database/Handle.hs:78:42 in main:Database.Handle\n\n\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505234625,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODkxMjM5Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328912397"},"message":"And `git annex version` returns the following\n\n```\n$ git annex version\ngit-annex version: 6.20170815+gitg22da64d0f-1~ndall+1\nbuild flags: Assistant Webapp Pairing Testsuite S3(multipartupload)(storageclasses) WebDAV Inotify DBus DesktopNotify ConcurrentOutput TorrentParser MagicMime Feeds Quvi\ndependency versions: aws-0.14.1 bloomfilter-2.0.1.0 cryptonite-0.20 DAV-1.3.1 feed-0.3.11.1 ghc-8.0.1 http-client-0.4.31.1 persistent-sqlite-2.6 torrent-10000.0.0 uuid-1.3.12 yesod-1.4.3\nkey/value backends: SHA256E SHA256 SHA512E SHA512 SHA224E SHA224 SHA384E SHA384 SHA3_256E SHA3_256 SHA3_512E SHA3_512 SHA3_224E SHA3_224 SHA3_384E SHA3_384 SKEIN256E SKEIN256 SKEIN512E SKEIN512 SHA1E SHA1 MD5E MD5 WORM URL\nremote types: git gcrypt p2p S3 bup directory rsync web bittorrent webdav tahoe glacier ddar hook external\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505235003,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODkxNDMyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328914327"},"message":"ah, apparently there is not good enough of logging (@joeyh would be nice to have more diagnostics output) to state why crippled\nbut looking at the code\n```haskell\nprobeCrippledFileSystem' :: FilePath -\u003e Annex Bool\n#ifdef mingw32_HOST_OS\nprobeCrippledFileSystem' _ = return True\n#else\nprobeCrippledFileSystem' tmp = do\n    let f = tmp \u003c/\u003e \"gaprobe\"\n    liftIO $ writeFile f \"\"\n    uncrippled \u003c- probe f\n    void $ liftIO $ tryIO $ allowWrite f\n    liftIO $ removeFile f\n    return $ not uncrippled\n  where\n    probe f = catchBoolIO $ do\n        let f2 = f ++ \"2\"\n        liftIO $ nukeFile f2\n        liftIO $ createSymbolicLink f f2\n        liftIO $ nukeFile f2\n        liftIO $ preventWrite f\n        -- Should be unable to write to the file, unless\n        -- running as root, but some crippled\n        -- filesystems ignore write bit removals.\n        ifM ((== 0) \u003c$\u003e liftIO getRealUserID)\n            ( return True\n            , do\n                r \u003c- liftIO $ catchBoolIO $\n                    writeFile f \"2\" \u003e\u003e return True\n                if r\n                    then do\n                        warning \"Filesystem allows writing to files whose write bit is not set.\"\n                        return False\n                    else return True\n```\nit suggests that another culprit could be if file system allows to modify read-only files.  Could you try\n\n```shell\n$\u003e echo 123 \u003e testfile; chmod a-w testfile; echo more \u003e\u003e testfile\nzsh: permission denied: testfile\n```\nwould you get the same permission denied message?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505235087,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODkxNDcxOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328914719"},"message":"also @joeyh could you please have a pick at [above crash message](https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328912049) from v6 mode and sqlite?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505235380,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODkxNjE4NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328916185"},"message":"I do not get that permission denied message when I run \n```\n$\u003e echo 123 \u003e testfile; chmod a-w testfile; echo more \u003e\u003e testfile\n```\nAnd then testfile contains \n```\n123\nmore\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505247305,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyODk3MTQwOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-328971409"},"message":"that is the problem :-/ -- in indirect mode (using symlinks to read-only files) git-annex relies on ability to \"protect\" data files from being modified... otherwise integrity could not be guaranteed and many things could go wrong.  So the only way for us would be to get v6 mode fixed up.  We had some [similarish (but different) looking issues](https://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/drop_blows_on_lustre__58___SQLite3_returned_ErrorIO/) while trying it awhile back on lustre as well  . \n\nI see that there were some sqlite related issues/fixes in git-annex since the version you are using... I do not see them directly related (from commit msgs) so unlikely they would help, but if you could try most recent development snapshot, it could be of great help so we could file an issue with git-annex as seek @joeyh help.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505312979,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTE4NTkxOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329185919"},"message":"Okay, this definitely seems like it's an issue with this specific filesystem, not AFP or its interactions with Ubuntu; I've recreated the problem on my machine when the server's mounted using sshfs and on a Mac using both sshfs and AFP. I'm trying to figure that issue out, but I guess if datalad supported v6 mode, then that should work too.  \n\nFor the second part of your comment, the most recent development snapshot would be installing git-annex from source, right? And then which part would you like me to re-run?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505314692,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTE5NTEyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329195128"},"message":"yes -- it has to do with the local layer ( afpfs-ng and gvfs-mount). would be nice to demo it on a simple case and let upstream of those projects know\n\nsnapshot -- ... right... you are using neurodebian already and the most recent one... although current snapshot builds, it doesn't pass the tests (already reported to @joeyh) which forbids generation of the package ATM.  so may be hold on for a bit\n\nthe question is then\n- do you have access to the AFP server directly? should probably just work there \n- or just use datalad locally on non AFP mounted partition","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505317200,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTIwODQ5NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329208494"},"message":"I'm not sure what you mean by access to the AFP server directly. I can ssh into it, but still have able to write to files I shouldn't have write access to problem there. \n\nI probably will end up using datalad to manage the copies of the data that aren't on the AFP server, but being able to use datalad for all locations would be easier, so I am going to see if I can figure out what's going on with the filesystem.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1505317269,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTIwODg2Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329208862"},"message":"Does the sqlite crash only happen when running git-annex in the\nfilesystem that has been giving other problem, or can you reproduce it\non a filesystem such as ext4?\n\n\u003e sqlite worker thread crashed: SQLite3 returned ErrorError while\n\u003e attempting to perform prepare \"SELECT null from content limit 1\": no\n\u003e such table: content\n\nThe content table is part of the keys database, which should be located\nat .git/annex/keys/db in the git repository. Running sqlite3 on that\nfile and then running the \".dump\" command should list two tables,\nincluding content. This error kind of looks like the database file\nexists but the table somehow does not, which I can't see how could\nhappen unless something seriously confused sqlite.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505317579,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTIxMDQzNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329210437"},"message":"This is almost certainly unrelated, but there's no `datalad run` in my datalad install. Running `datalad run` with any command prints the following\n\n```\nusage: datalad [-h] [-l LEVEL] [--pbs-runner {condor}] [-C PATH] [--version]\n               [--dbg] [--idbg] [-c KEY=VALUE]\n               [--output-format {default,json,json_pp,tailored,'\u003ctemplate\u003e']\n               [--report-status {success,failure,ok,notneeded,impossible,error}]\n               [--report-type {dataset,file}]\n               [--on-failure {ignore,continue,stop}]\n               [--run-before PLUGINSPEC [PLUGINSPEC ...]]\n               [--run-after PLUGINSPEC [PLUGINSPEC ...]] [--cmd]\n               {create,install,get,add,publish,uninstall,drop,remove,update,create-sibling,create-sibling-github,unlock,save,plugin,search,metadata,aggregate-metadata,test,crawl,crawl-init,ls,clean,add-archive-content,download-url,annotate-paths,clone,create-test-dataset,diff,siblings,sshrun,subdatasets}\n               ...\ndatalad: error: invalid choice: 'run' (choose from 'create', 'install', 'get', 'add', 'publish', 'uninstall', 'drop', 'remove', 'update', 'create-sibling', 'create-sibling-github', 'unlock', 'save', 'plugin', 'search', 'metadata', 'aggregate-metadata', 'test', 'crawl', 'crawl-init', 'ls', 'clean', 'add-archive-content', 'download-url', 'annotate-paths', 'clone', 'create-test-dataset', 'diff', 'siblings', 'sshrun', 'subdatasets')\n```\n\nAnd my datalad version is 0.8.1, installed from neurodebian. I get the same thing if I installed datalad using pip.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505317742,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTIxMTMzNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329211336"},"message":"@joeyh I've only had the sqlite crash when running git-annex in the filesystem that has been giving the other problem, I can't reproduce it elsewhere.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505318793,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTIxNjYzOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329216638"},"message":"re `run` -- it was added just recently... we are plowing forward to release 0.9.0 asap, but still there is few more issues to fix.  will come out within few days.  With pip you could install directly from github: `pip install git+http://github.com/datalad/datalad` but I would advise to do that in a virtualenv so you could later just disable it and install recent one from neurodebian pkg","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1505320767,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTIyNTk4MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329225981"},"message":"William F. Broderick wrote:\n\u003e @joeyh I've only had the sqlite crash when running git-annex in the filesystem\n\u003e that has been giving the other problem, I can't reproduce it elsewhere.\n\nDoes the .git/annex/keys/db sqlite database exist after the crash?\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505332043,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTI3NjczNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329276735"},"message":"@yarikoptic Okay, I'll wait for 0.9.0 to be released then.\n\n@joeyh I'm actually no longer having that sqlite crash issue, weirdly. I didn't change anything on my end, but the IT people at my department are looking into the server, so it's possible they've changed something. They should be finished by tomorrow, so I can double-check then to see if the issue is still happening.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505400950,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTUwODQ2Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329508466"},"message":"The permissions issue was fixed on the server, so that `$\u003e echo 123 \u003e testfile; chmod a-w testfile; echo more \u003e\u003e testfile` raises an error as expected, and now datalad works as expected, both with `DATALAD_REPO_VERSION=6` and without.\n\nThanks for your help!","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505400950,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTI0OTM5MDIyMw=="},"status":2},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505401428,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTUxMTEwMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-329511103"},"message":"That is awesome @billbrod -- thanks for making it happen.  Do you know any detail on how it was fixed on the server side, and which client side ( afpfs-ng or gvfs-mount)  you ended up using which allowed to work in indirect (not v6) mode?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505405096,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTUzMDAzMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment