es.list \n# NeuroDebian -devel repository\ndeb     http://neuro.debian.net/debian-devel stretch main contrib non-free\ndeb-src http://neuro.debian.net/debian-devel stretch main contrib non-free\n```\nLet us know if this one fails the same way.\n\nnote (from your last msg I got suspicion) that once you upgraded repository to v6 -- that is it, you would not be able to use it in regular indirect way.  Do you have now two copies -- one in indirect and one in v6?  whenever cut/pasting output, also include original command as you typed it in shell (like I did above) -- could help to identify confusion/culprit.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1505769906,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDM2MDkzNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-330360936"},"message":"Thanks @yarikoptic . Somehow the write permission issue has re-appeared (that is `$\u003e echo 123 \u003e testfile; chmod a-w testfile; echo more \u003e\u003e testfile` does not raise permission denied error), so the issues from earlier have re-surfaced. Hopefully we'll get that figured out soon and then I'll see if my other issue appears as well (I have updated my datalad to the version in the debian-devel repo).\n\nSorry about the confusion (I'll include the command from now on) -- those were all done in clean repos, after I had unset `DATALAD_REPO_VERSION`, so that I'm pretty sure it was working in the regular indirect way.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505778895,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDM4ODUwMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-330388501"},"message":"Thank you @billbrod for not giving up. Please later share what was done on the AFP server side to mitigate it.\nCheers","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505804082,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDQ0NzEwMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-330447101"},"message":"\u003e Sorry about the confusion (I'll include the command from now on) -- those were all done in clean repos, after I had unset DATALAD_REPO_VERSION, so that I'm pretty sure it was working in the regular indirect way.\n\nReading this, I'm not sure whether you are aware @billbrod . Therefore please note: `DATALAD_REPO_VERSION` just defines the default to use when creating (or installing) a new dataset. The version used by an annex repository is a property of that repository. So, once created using v6, it remains a v6 repository even if you unset `DATALAD_REPO_VERSION`. You can inspect the repository version if you have a look at its `.git/config` file (section `[annex]` has an entry `version = ...`).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1557434104,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5MTA1NjE4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-491056183"},"message":"@billbrod - is there anything we could/should do on datalad side or this issue could be closed?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1557434330,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5MTA1NzM2Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-491057366"},"message":"I think this can be closed, I'm don't think there's any thing to be done on the datalad side","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"7b1dbae6a61e68ec982b5b7514c7b37f8adb923b"},"timestamp":1557434330,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjMzMTM5NjExMA=="},"status":2},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1557454599,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5MTEyOTcwMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1825#issuecomment-491129700"},"message":"thank you @billbrod !","files":null}]}